ef 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524883 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524883 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524883 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186524801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524883 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "662d422b-1530-5ba0-98a4-0880cce3feef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524908 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524449 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524908 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524908 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524908 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524908 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524736 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524908 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524908 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524908 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186524449 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524908 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9776b31f-8640-5e03-aee4-a9445951e6de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524979 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524863 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524979 #edb/ref 1069 "q-70398" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524979 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524979 #edb/ref 1071 "The point $P$ with coordinates $(1,3)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which of the following points must lie on $y=f(x+4)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524979 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "39cdb9cb-c996-510c-9952-40829263e555" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524979 #edb/ref 1074 "The graph of $y=f(x+4)$ is a translation of the graph of $y=f(x)$ by $4$ units to the *left*. So the $y$-coordinate remains unchanged while the $x$-coordinate decreases by $4.$\n\nWe know that the point $(1,3)$ lies on $y=f(x).$ Therefore, the point $(1-4,3)=(-3,3)$ must lie on $y=f(x+4).$\n\n![](images/2a/2a7333b3778aed3b4a9d744c6a100577fdeeafc497ac9d7f33670908163551b2.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524981 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524981 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110268" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524981 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524981 #edb/ref 1071 "The point $P$ with coordinates $(1,2)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which of the following points must lie on $y=f(x+5)+2?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524981 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "44298347-9f79-536a-ae21-5b66403bb6c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524981 #edb/ref 1074 "The graph of $y=f(x+5)+2$  is a translation of the graph of $y=f(x)$ by $5$ units to the *left* and $2$ units up. So the $y$-coordinate increases by $2$ and the $x$-coordinate decreases by $5.$\n\nWe know that the point $(1,2)$ lies on $y=f(x).$ Therefore, the point $(1-5,2+2)=(-4,4)$ must lie on $y=f(x+5)+2.$\n\n![](images/00/00557550846a020f437c6187dfe237b4e1cb874eca2bb1cf2bd70416e0e8d97c.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525008 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525008 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72294" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525008 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525008 #edb/ref 1071 "The point $P$ with coordinates $(0,3)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which of the following points must lie on $y=f(x-1)-2?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525008 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8c7a6d9e-5cbe-57ca-9331-32f4ca36decb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525008 #edb/ref 1074 "The graph of $y=f(x-1)-2$ is a translation of the graph of $y=f(x)$ by $1$ unit to the *right* and $2$ units *down*. So the $y$-coordinate decreases by $2$ and the $x$-coordinate increases by $1.$\n\nWe know that the point $(0,3)$ lies on $y=f(x).$ Therefore, the point $(0+1,3-2)=(1,1)$ must lie on $y=f(x-1)-2.$\n\n![](images/64/64d0dc944682b12702eb8a2fa9de0ef3e65cc57ac1cc7a242a09c986ca7f955c.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525020 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524879 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525020 #edb/ref 1069 "q-70399" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525020 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525020 #edb/ref 1071 "The point $P$ with coordinates $(1,1)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which of the following points must lie on $y=f(x-4)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525020 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9f46143b-fdb8-50df-bf49-6caa0060fc7f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525020 #edb/ref 1074 "The graph of $y=f(x-4)$ is a translation of the graph of $y=f(x)$ by $4$ units to the *right*. So the $y$-coordinate remains unchanged while the $x$-coordinate increases by $4.$\n\nWe know that the point $(1,1)$ lies on $y=f(x).$ Therefore, the point $(1+4,1)=(5,1)$ must lie on $y=f(x-4).$\n\n![](images/8c/8c736b4ad424cfc7efe3cd7218f873655b5bface8fe4cc670b8185ff1b73f5e5.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525037 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525037 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110147" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525037 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525037 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/7b/7b89a8737e3fcb062d5cb53a8832bc3d8f30273696b3be0e8c47d25ba158fa60.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the graphs of $y=f(x)$ and $y=g(x)$, where $g(x)=f(x+a)+b.$ What are the values of $a$ and $b?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525037 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c3371da1-431a-54c0-b96b-91167f5060d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525037 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that every point on the graph $y=g(x)$ is three units *to the left* and two units *up* of the corresponding point on the graph of $y=f(x).$ \n\nSo, we conclude that $g(x)=f(x+3)+2,$ and therefore $a=3$ and $b=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525060 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525060 #edb/ref 1069 "q-34672" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525060 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525060 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/b8/b8a944368cb4549780c5868c164a57d55fffff205ef0816b7316cb9fcf5a93dc.png)\n\nGiven the curve $y=f(x)$ and the curve $y=f(x+a)$, which of the following is the value of $a?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525060 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f10d9718-f09b-5a57-a9a5-0bd402337019" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525060 #edb/ref 1074 "Every point on the graph of $y=f(x+a)$ is $2$ units *to the left* of the corresponding point on the graph of $y=f(x).$ So the graph of $y=f(x+a)$ is a horizontal translation of the graph of $y=f(x)$ by $2$ units to the *left*. \n\nConsequently, $y=f(x+a)=f(x+2)$ and so $a=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
